-- title:
--   Spreading a finite flat algebra over a local ring to a basic open
-- statement:
--   Let $S$ be a noetherian commutative ring and $\mathfrak p$ a point of $\operatorname{Spec} S$, with associated prime ideal $\mathfrak p$ and local ring $S_{\mathfrak p}$ (the localisation of $S$ at $\mathfrak p$). Let $C_0$ be a commutative ring which is simultaneously an $S$-algebra and an $S_{\mathfrak p}$-algebra, compatibly, so that $S \to S_{\mathfrak p} \to C_0$ is the structure map, and assume $C_0$ is finite as an $S_{\mathfrak p}$-module and faithfully flat as an $S_{\mathfrak p}$-module. Then there exist an element $g \in S$ with $g \notin \mathfrak p$ and a commutative ring $C$, equipped with an $S$-algebra structure and an $S_g$-algebra structure (where $S_g$ is the localisation of $S$ away from $g$) compatible with $S \to S_g$, together with a $C$-algebra structure on $C_0$ compatible with the $S$-algebra structures of $C$ and $C_0$, such that $C$ is finite, free, faithfully flat and of finite presentation as an $S_g$-algebra (respectively module), and such that $C_0$ is a localisation of $C$ at the multiplicative set generated by the image in $C$ of the complement $S \setminus \mathfrak p$; equivalently $C_0 \cong C \otimes_{S_g} S_{\mathfrak p}$.
--
--   This is the standard spreading-out step: a finite faithfully flat algebra over the local ring $S_{\mathfrak p}$ is free, and its finitely many structure constants can be realised over a basic open neighbourhood $\operatorname{Spec} S_g$ of $\mathfrak p$. It is used in the construction of principal square roots and symmetric data for abelian schemes, where a finite faithfully flat algebra carrying such data over the local ring at $\mathfrak p$ must be descended to an open neighbourhood before the data are spread out.
